  "name": null,
  "problem": "Find the moment ${M}_{x}$ of the plate about the $x$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${M}_{x}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={\u222c}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $\\lambda (x,y)=2x{y}^{2}$ and the plate occupies the region\n\n$$\nD={(x,y):0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={\u222c}_{D}y\\cdot 2x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}2x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}2x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{3}{[{x}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{3}({3}^{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}9{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{9}{4}{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}(2)^{4}-0 \\\\  & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
